 146:Middlewares/Third_Party/LibJPEG/source/jdatasrc.c **** /*
 147:Middlewares/Third_Party/LibJPEG/source/jdatasrc.c ****  * Skip data --- used to skip over a potentially large amount of
 148:Middlewares/Third_Party/LibJPEG/source/jdatasrc.c ****  * uninteresting data (such as an APPn marker).
 149:Middlewares/Third_Party/LibJPEG/source/jdatasrc.c ****  *
 150:Middlewares/Third_Party/LibJPEG/source/jdatasrc.c ****  * Writers of suspendable-input applications must note that skip_input_data
 151:Middlewares/Third_Party/LibJPEG/source/jdatasrc.c ****  * is not granted the right to give a suspension return.  If the skip extends
 152:Middlewares/Third_Party/LibJPEG/source/jdatasrc.c ****  * beyond the data currently in the buffer, the buffer can be marked empty so
 153:Middlewares/Third_Party/LibJPEG/source/jdatasrc.c ****  * that the next read will cause a fill_input_buffer call that can suspend.
 154:Middlewares/Third_Party/LibJPEG/source/jdatasrc.c ****  * Arranging for additional bytes to be discarded before reloading the input
 155:Middlewares/Third_Party/LibJPEG/source/jdatasrc.c ****  * buffer is the application writer's problem.
 156:Middlewares/Third_Party/LibJPEG/source/jdatasrc.c ****  */
